WEBVTT

00:01.760 --> 00:04.558
Hey, Berta, how have you been
washing my underwear?

00:04.720 --> 00:06.551
Like I do everything else around here:

00:06.720 --> 00:09.439
With a song on my lips
and love in my heart.

00:11.080 --> 00:12.354
I'm serious.

00:12.520 --> 00:14.954
I got a rash in my, you know,
private area.

00:16.080 --> 00:19.516
Private? You get more traffic
you're gonna have to open a Starbucks.

00:22.240 --> 00:24.231
I thought maybe
you'd changed laundry soap...

00:24.400 --> 00:26.755
...because it's all red and itchy,
especially around...

00:26.920 --> 00:28.148
Excuse me.

00:29.600 --> 00:32.637
I'm sitting here
eating a breakfast sausage.

00:34.280 --> 00:36.748
It's not a sausage problem.

00:36.920 --> 00:38.717
It's more in the meatball area.

00:42.160 --> 00:45.197
Kind of meatball adjacent.

00:46.000 --> 00:47.228
I bet it's swamp ass.

00:49.000 --> 00:50.069
What's swamp ass?

00:50.240 --> 00:52.879
Don't worry,
you'd know if you had swamp ass.

00:53.040 --> 00:55.315
Man, I hate swamp ass.

00:55.840 --> 00:58.513
- You sure it's just a rash?
- What else could it be?

00:58.680 --> 01:00.352
Since we're talking about your area...

01:00.520 --> 01:03.512
...it could be anything
from Ebola to mad cow disease.

01:04.080 --> 01:05.593
You get Ebola from monkeys, right?

01:05.760 --> 01:06.795
Right.

01:07.640 --> 01:08.914
It's just a rash.

01:10.480 --> 01:13.995
A kid at school got swamp ass.
Cats followed him around for a year.

01:15.160 --> 01:19.119
- You know what? Let's forget about it.
- Oh, if only we could.

01:19.280 --> 01:21.589
Speaking of school,
we've got a big day ahead of us.

01:21.760 --> 01:23.512
Gotta go shopping for supplies, clothes.

01:24.120 --> 01:25.678
Nice segue, Dad.

01:25.840 --> 01:28.877
Well, the subject was crying out
for change.

01:29.040 --> 01:31.634
You're starting a new school.
You're gonna need new stuff.

01:31.800 --> 01:35.110
Wait a sec.
Melon Head made it into junior high?

01:35.280 --> 01:38.397
- Yes.
- So you passed summer school?

01:38.560 --> 01:40.949
- Sort of.
- What do you mean "sort of"?

01:41.120 --> 01:43.998
They said it was in everyone's
best interest if I moved on.

01:45.880 --> 01:46.869
What's that mean?

01:47.040 --> 01:48.837
Promoted him.
He's starting junior high.

01:49.000 --> 01:52.276
And there's absolutely nothing
to be gained in asking how or why.

01:53.440 --> 01:55.590
Okay, well, whatever.
I'm proud of you, man.

01:56.080 --> 01:57.559
- For what?
- I don't know...

01:57.720 --> 01:59.915
...hanging in there
till they were sick of you.

02:00.080 --> 02:01.593
Thanks.

02:02.960 --> 02:05.110
So junior high, huh?

02:05.280 --> 02:07.430
Boy, that brings back some memories,
doesn't it?

02:08.400 --> 02:10.072
Can we please not go down that road?

02:10.240 --> 02:11.275
What happened?

02:11.440 --> 02:15.149
Nothing. It's just that kids
in junior high can be a little judgmental.

02:15.680 --> 02:17.432
Especially if you're knocked up.

02:21.680 --> 02:23.272
Thank you, Berta.

02:23.440 --> 02:25.317
Of course, on the upside...

02:25.480 --> 02:28.313
...the pregnant chicks
didn't have to go to gym.

02:28.480 --> 02:33.110
Did the guys who got them pregnant get
considerations? No, not even a hall pass.

02:34.320 --> 02:35.673
Are we quite done?

02:37.280 --> 02:38.554
Things will go great for you.

02:38.720 --> 02:41.109
- You just have to remember a few things.
- Like what?

02:41.280 --> 02:43.589
Well, always keep
your lunch money in your shoe...

02:43.760 --> 02:45.751
...but have some spare change
in your pocket.

02:45.920 --> 02:47.114
- How come?
- Decoy money.

02:47.280 --> 02:49.589
They won't stop hitting you
till they get something.

02:50.840 --> 02:51.829
Who are "they"?

02:52.000 --> 02:54.958
The kids holding your ankles,
plunging your head in the toilet.

02:56.480 --> 02:57.913
Plunging my head in the toilet?

02:58.080 --> 03:01.197
Don't freak the kid out, Alan.

03:01.360 --> 03:03.920
It's not so much plunging as dipping.

03:05.120 --> 03:06.394
Here's what you do:

03:06.560 --> 03:09.552
Make friends with the janitor.
They usually have their own bathroom.

03:10.840 --> 03:13.559
- Okay.
- Just never drink out of his Thermos.

03:14.800 --> 03:15.789
All right.

03:15.960 --> 03:17.712
And don't believe he loves you.

03:21.200 --> 03:23.760
Damn it,
I miss that one-eyed son of a bitch.

03:27.800 --> 03:29.756
And if you have to shower
after gym class...

03:29.920 --> 03:32.434
...there is no shame
in keeping your jockey shorts on.

03:33.480 --> 03:35.198
- Really?
- Okay, there's a little shame.

03:36.960 --> 03:40.077
The important thing is the fellas
won't be calling you Shrinky Dink.

03:42.080 --> 03:45.197
- Shrinky Dink?
- I'm a grower, not a shower.

03:47.600 --> 03:49.511
Oh, I almost forgot.

03:50.240 --> 03:52.674
I got you a little present.

03:52.840 --> 03:55.752
- Your very own cell phone.
- Oh, cool.

03:55.920 --> 03:58.229
The important thing
to remember is this is not a toy.

03:58.400 --> 04:01.995
- It's to use in emergencies only.
- Emergencies? What emergencies?

04:02.160 --> 04:03.593
"Dad, come get me.

04:04.160 --> 04:07.516
I'm stuffed in my locker
and my underwear is wet."

04:15.840 --> 04:17.592
That only happened once.

04:18.640 --> 04:21.598
If that dog hadn't found you,
you'd have missed Thanksgiving.

04:23.160 --> 04:26.197
- Drug-sniffing dog?
- There were no drugs.

04:26.720 --> 04:29.837
That's true. Turns out those dogs
are also sensitive to urine.

04:31.720 --> 04:33.756
I was in there for five hours.

04:34.400 --> 04:35.833
Five hours?

04:36.320 --> 04:39.790
But you don't have to worry about that.
You have a cell phone.

04:40.880 --> 04:44.156
Which you should hide where
prisoners of war hid their watches.

04:45.320 --> 04:47.834
- Where was that?
- Moving on.

04:48.000 --> 04:49.274
I've preprogrammed the phone:

04:49.440 --> 04:51.874
Speed dial one is me,
two is the nurse's office...

04:52.040 --> 04:53.553
...and three is the police.

04:54.560 --> 04:55.754
The police? What for?

04:55.920 --> 04:57.831
You'll know it when it happens.

04:58.000 --> 04:59.319
Now, about race riots...

04:59.480 --> 05:02.392
- Try not to take sides.
- Anybody asks, you're mulatto.

05:33.480 --> 05:36.040
- How do they feel?
- Okay, but they're ugly.

05:36.200 --> 05:37.872
They look like old-people shoes.

05:38.040 --> 05:40.349
They're not old-people shoes.
They're walking shoes.

05:40.520 --> 05:44.274
Right, for people
who've been walking for 85 years.

05:44.440 --> 05:46.590
I'd rather get these. These are cool.

05:46.760 --> 05:49.194
Listen, junior high
is not about being cool.

05:49.360 --> 05:51.794
It's about
not getting mugged for sneakers.

05:51.960 --> 05:54.110
I can get mugged for my sneakers?

05:54.280 --> 05:56.350
Not those sneakers.

05:57.520 --> 05:59.875
Not unless you go by
an assisted-living facility...

06:00.040 --> 06:01.393
...in a rough neighborhood.

06:03.080 --> 06:04.069
What are you doing?

06:08.720 --> 06:11.518
I'm sorry. This rash is driving me crazy.

06:11.680 --> 06:13.352
I feel stupid in these.

06:13.520 --> 06:15.909
Better to feel stupid
than to be tied to a flagpole...

06:16.080 --> 06:18.435
...while upperclassmen
use you as a spittoon.

06:18.600 --> 06:20.556
I don't wanna be tied to a flagpole.

06:20.720 --> 06:23.792
You won't be. Wear the ugly shoes
and don't sit at the wrong table.

06:23.960 --> 06:26.918
Wrong table?
How will I know if it's the wrong table?

06:27.080 --> 06:29.992
You'll be tied to a flagpole, right, Alan?

06:30.760 --> 06:33.672
That also only happened once.

06:34.640 --> 06:36.790
Let's just check the fit.

06:37.600 --> 06:39.158
Good.

06:39.320 --> 06:40.833
Plenty of room for lunch money.

06:47.600 --> 06:49.397
How come all my clothes
have to be beige?

06:49.560 --> 06:52.791
Because beige is not the color
of any known gang.

06:52.960 --> 06:55.474
Right, instead of being mistaken
for a Crip or a Blood...

06:55.640 --> 06:57.437
...you'll be mistaken for a Band-Aid.

06:57.920 --> 07:00.309
Hey, Band-Aids are ouchless.

07:03.840 --> 07:05.558
Excuse me? Excuse me, there's a line.

07:06.080 --> 07:08.548
- Yeah, I just got a couple of things.
- I can see that...

07:08.720 --> 07:10.631
...but it's not based
on quantity of items.

07:10.800 --> 07:13.633
It's more of a
"we were here before you" kind of deal.

07:15.800 --> 07:17.631
You gonna make a thing out of this?

07:19.080 --> 07:22.117
There's no thing.
Just playing by the rules.

07:22.280 --> 07:25.033
And wouldn't it be nice
if everybody did the same?

07:25.640 --> 07:26.675
Hang on to this, slick.

07:28.360 --> 07:31.113
Now, you wanna explain
those rules again, jughead?

07:33.160 --> 07:35.879
You know what? If you're in a hurry,
why don't you go ahead?

07:36.480 --> 07:37.469
Thank you.

07:39.760 --> 07:41.432
What the hell are you doing?

07:43.640 --> 07:44.914
Nothing. Here.

07:50.120 --> 07:52.270
No, no, not chicken.
Just good common sense.

07:52.440 --> 07:56.592
- Fighting accomplishes nothing.
- Oh, I didn't know you were so French.

07:57.640 --> 07:59.312
- Hey.
- Oh, hey, Julie.

08:01.000 --> 08:03.036
How do you know my wife?

08:03.480 --> 08:06.233
What? Oh, no, no, no, I don't know her.

08:06.680 --> 08:08.159
You said, "Hey, Julie."

08:08.640 --> 08:11.791
No, no, I sneezed.

08:15.800 --> 08:17.950
- Gesundheit.
- Thank you.

08:18.560 --> 08:21.950
Oh, look, another cashier opened up.
Let's go, let's go, let's go.

08:27.560 --> 08:29.710
But Mom said I could wait
for the bus by myself.

08:29.880 --> 08:31.233
I know.

08:31.400 --> 08:33.595
I would really rather wait
for the bus by myself.

08:33.760 --> 08:35.796
I just wanna make sure
you get off okay.

08:35.960 --> 08:38.713
Yeah, but being walked to the bus stop
by my dad and my uncle?

08:38.880 --> 08:40.518
I'm gonna look so lame.

08:40.680 --> 08:43.752
Jake, buddy, that ship has sailed.

08:49.920 --> 08:51.876
Please don't leave me.

08:52.680 --> 08:55.717
You're okay.
Just don't make eye contact.

08:57.160 --> 09:00.357
Okay, when the bus comes,
don't take a window seat.

09:00.520 --> 09:02.988
You don't wanna be trapped
and get pummeled.

09:03.160 --> 09:04.957
- Pummeled?
- And be polite to the driver.

09:05.120 --> 09:07.554
They tend to be damaged people
with short fuses.

09:07.720 --> 09:09.756
- Fuses?
- Don't distract him.

09:10.320 --> 09:11.548
There's no seat belts.

09:11.720 --> 09:14.439
One sharp turn, and you kids
will be flying like lotto balls.

09:14.600 --> 09:16.511
Balls?

09:20.040 --> 09:21.951
Wait, wait, wait.

09:23.880 --> 09:25.996
- Smile.
- About what?

09:26.160 --> 09:28.390
I need a current picture
in case you go missing.

09:28.560 --> 09:31.711
Alan, you're being ridiculous.
They never find those kids.

09:31.880 --> 09:33.711
Give me a profile.

09:35.080 --> 09:38.152
Okay, now go make it a great day.

09:39.200 --> 09:40.235
Have fun.

09:56.840 --> 09:58.910
I just hope everything turns out all right.

09:59.080 --> 10:03.392
Well, we've done all we could.
Now it's up to him.

10:15.240 --> 10:16.355
Okay. Okay.

10:16.520 --> 10:18.476
Tell the doctor that if I was a tree...

10:18.640 --> 10:22.474
...the rash is predominantly
around the mossy trunk area.

10:28.200 --> 10:32.079
But I'm starting to see some redness
on the adjacent boulders.

10:33.640 --> 10:34.629
Oh, come on.

10:34.800 --> 10:37.439
Tree, two boulders,
what part don't you understand?

10:38.800 --> 10:39.949
- Hey.
- Hey.

10:40.120 --> 10:42.350
Okay, just have him call me.

10:42.520 --> 10:43.999
- Heard from Jake?
- Nope.

10:44.160 --> 10:46.628
I'll call him at his mom's,
see how school went.

10:46.800 --> 10:50.076
- Alan, does this look infected to you?
- What?

10:50.640 --> 10:51.993
Get that away from me.

10:52.160 --> 10:54.469
I'm not asking you to tickle it.
Just take a look.

10:54.640 --> 10:55.914
No, thank you.

10:56.080 --> 10:57.354
But you're a doctor.

10:57.520 --> 11:00.990
I'm a chiropractor.
I work with vertebrae.

11:01.160 --> 11:05.039
And contrary to popular belief,
there is not a single bone in the penis.

11:06.120 --> 11:07.838
Oh, hi, Judith.

11:08.880 --> 11:10.791
Nothing. I was just talking to Charlie.

11:10.960 --> 11:13.394
Hey, hey, is Jake home
from school yet?

11:13.560 --> 11:14.834
No?

11:15.000 --> 11:17.195
Okay, I was just
wondering how his first day went.

11:17.360 --> 11:20.875
Have him call me, okay?
Thanks, bye-bye.

11:22.400 --> 11:24.630
Hope he didn't wander
under bleachers during lunch.

11:24.800 --> 11:27.758
- He's smarter than that.
- Smart?

11:27.920 --> 11:31.071
He only got out of sixth grade
because he couldn't fit in the desks.

11:32.280 --> 11:34.589
If you're that concerned,
just call him on his cell.

11:34.960 --> 11:36.552
Good idea.

11:51.560 --> 11:54.632
Jake? Jake, where are you?

11:56.560 --> 11:59.028
You're still on the bus.

12:02.160 --> 12:04.390
Funny, I don't hear the other kids.

12:04.560 --> 12:07.120
Oh, yeah, it was a tough day.
Everybody's tired.

12:09.120 --> 12:10.109
No kidding.

12:11.920 --> 12:14.388
Dad, this phone
is for emergencies only.

12:16.840 --> 12:18.319
Why aren't you at your mother's?

12:18.480 --> 12:21.358
I got off the bus at school,
got on another bus and came here.

12:21.520 --> 12:24.751
- So you've never been to school today?
- Of course not.

12:24.920 --> 12:28.959
I don't wanna be stuffed in a locker,
tied to a flagpole or dunked in a toilet.

12:29.920 --> 12:31.911
Not dunked. Dipped.

12:32.720 --> 12:36.633
- And where are your new sneakers?
- Oh, I sold them to the bus driver.

12:43.760 --> 12:45.432
Charlie, can I talk to you a minute?

12:46.840 --> 12:49.479
- Are those my comics?
- Charlie.

12:50.560 --> 12:53.438
They're near mint
and he wipes his boogers all over them.

12:54.160 --> 12:55.957
He was here all day
and you didn't know?

12:56.120 --> 12:58.588
Hey, I've got a rash.

13:00.480 --> 13:03.119
I can't believe he cut school
on his first day.

13:03.280 --> 13:05.191
When you think about it,
it's pretty smart.

13:05.360 --> 13:08.158
As far as the school is concerned,
he might just be a typo.

13:09.280 --> 13:11.430
Charlie, the question
is why did he cut school?

13:11.600 --> 13:12.749
Oh, that's easy.

13:12.920 --> 13:15.992
You scared the crap out of him
and dressed him like an ace bandage.

13:16.160 --> 13:18.151
Hey, hey,
I was just trying to prepare him.

13:18.320 --> 13:20.550
For what? A life of running and hiding?

13:20.720 --> 13:22.119
No, no, a life of blending in.

13:22.280 --> 13:24.077
Only if they see you,
running and hiding.

13:25.520 --> 13:28.239
Face it, Alan. When the lord
was handing out courage...

13:28.400 --> 13:30.914
...you were crouched in a locker,
peeing on your socks.

13:32.400 --> 13:37.633
Okay, first of all,
I had had three Mr. Pibb's at lunch.

13:37.800 --> 13:39.597
And secondly, I am not a coward.

13:39.760 --> 13:42.479
Come on. I've seen steelier nerves
from a cat on the freeway.

13:43.280 --> 13:44.713
That's ridiculous.

13:45.840 --> 13:47.671
Dingo.

13:48.480 --> 13:52.029
Okay, I was not ready and that was
not fair. And what about you?

13:52.800 --> 13:54.791
- What about me?
- You're afraid of everything.

13:54.960 --> 13:57.428
- Like what?
- Well, let's see.

13:57.600 --> 13:59.591
Germs, change,
opening your eyes underwater...

13:59.760 --> 14:03.070
...angry husbands, angry ex-girlfriends,
large birds, spiders and Mom.

14:04.120 --> 14:05.314
Hold on.

14:05.480 --> 14:07.232
Hold on a sec.

14:07.400 --> 14:10.756
I am not afraid to open my eyes
underwater, I'm just sensitive to chlorine.

14:11.320 --> 14:12.958
- Right.
- And for the record...

14:13.120 --> 14:14.712
...it's just when birds get indoors.

14:14.880 --> 14:16.711
In the sky, I got no problem.

14:17.400 --> 14:19.277
Fine, fine. Live in denial.

14:19.440 --> 14:21.112
I'm gonna straighten my kid out.

14:22.120 --> 14:25.874
And what sane person
is not afraid of spiders?

14:28.720 --> 14:31.518
What I'm trying to say
is that it was wrong to fill your head...

14:31.680 --> 14:34.114
...with a lot of horrible things
to avoid at school.

14:34.280 --> 14:36.430
Because the truth is
you can't avoid any of them.

14:36.600 --> 14:37.589
Charlie.

14:37.760 --> 14:39.432
You don't want him living in fear.

14:39.600 --> 14:42.239
- Well, yeah, but I was...
- Well, scary things happen in life.

14:42.400 --> 14:44.152
- He can hide like you...
- Like us.

14:44.320 --> 14:46.470
Don't nitpick.

14:46.640 --> 14:48.915
Or you can stand up to them.

14:49.080 --> 14:51.150
I mean, look,
getting hit in the face hurts.

14:51.320 --> 14:54.118
- But you know what hurts more?
- A kick in the crotch?

14:57.120 --> 14:58.712
Well, yeah, sure.

14:58.880 --> 15:02.395
I took a soccer ball to the nads once,
thought my eyes were gonna pop out.

15:08.360 --> 15:11.352
Yeah, but that pain passes.

15:11.520 --> 15:13.670
What hurts more
and lasts longer than anything...

15:13.840 --> 15:15.671
...is the humiliation of running away.

15:15.840 --> 15:17.831
I couldn't ride my bike for a week.

15:19.040 --> 15:21.156
Jake, I think you're missing the point.

15:21.320 --> 15:24.596
Makes you wonder what they're doing
hanging down there in the first place.

15:25.800 --> 15:28.314
No, what I think Uncle Charlie
is trying to say...

15:28.480 --> 15:31.870
...is that, yeah, you might get hit,
you might get stuffed in a locker...

15:32.040 --> 15:34.634
...but you know what? You'll survive.

15:34.800 --> 15:37.837
You may get bruised, you may bleed,
you may lose a few teeth...

15:38.000 --> 15:40.912
...but you'll have your self-respect.

15:41.080 --> 15:43.992
- Exactly.
- How do you stop being afraid?

15:46.960 --> 15:47.995
Well, I drink.

15:56.680 --> 15:59.240
But I didn't start till ninth grade.

16:04.960 --> 16:08.430
Yeah, Judith.
He was at Charlie's the whole time.

16:08.600 --> 16:12.388
Well, he said
he was too scared to go to school.

16:14.640 --> 16:17.438
How should I know why he's so scared?

16:17.600 --> 16:20.273
Maybe you're overprotective.

16:20.440 --> 16:21.475
Good one.

16:23.440 --> 16:25.590
I know you mean well.

16:25.760 --> 16:27.796
Oh, all right.
We'll be there in a few minutes.

16:27.960 --> 16:30.155
Okay. Bye-bye.

16:30.320 --> 16:32.231
- Did you hear that?
- Yeah, it's Mom's fault.

16:32.400 --> 16:34.038
Attaboy.

16:37.400 --> 16:40.358
Come on, it's green. Let's go.

16:43.840 --> 16:46.308
What's the matter with this guy?

16:49.760 --> 16:51.876
Looks like he's coming to tell you.

16:53.640 --> 16:55.790
Lock your doors. Lock your doors.

16:57.160 --> 17:00.550
Wait, no, no, wait.
I am tired of running and hiding.

17:00.720 --> 17:02.950
- Are you tired of running and hiding?
- Yes, I am.

17:03.440 --> 17:06.352
Remember, Jake,
courage is not the absence of fear...

17:06.520 --> 17:08.636
...it's taking action despite fear.

17:08.800 --> 17:10.870
That's very true.

17:14.520 --> 17:16.875
- Let's do this.
- Right behind you.

17:24.000 --> 17:26.070
Two against one wouldn't be fair.

17:29.360 --> 17:33.911
Now, that's courage.
Aren't you proud of him?

17:34.080 --> 17:35.559
You got your cell phone?

17:35.720 --> 17:37.438
It's only for emergencies.

17:39.640 --> 17:41.631
Help me.

17:42.800 --> 17:45.109
I think this qualifies.

17:46.800 --> 17:49.109
Charlie, Charlie, Charlie.

17:53.880 --> 17:56.599
- Hello?
- Hi.

17:58.200 --> 18:00.714
Charlie. Charlie.

18:11.040 --> 18:13.759
You are a bad brother.

18:13.920 --> 18:15.399
I really thought you had him.

18:16.800 --> 18:19.872
Mr. Harper, try not to sneeze.
You'll blow those stitches right out.

18:20.040 --> 18:21.598
Thank you, doctor.

18:21.760 --> 18:25.150
Hey, doc, while I got you here,
let me show you something.

18:27.080 --> 18:29.878
